# One line-ending convention (09 #18).
#
# Half the JS in this repo was committed CRLF and half LF, so a single
# line-ending flip has already shown up as a 9,130-line diff on
# js/xstitch.js, burying the ~50 lines that actually changed. Text files are
# normalised to LF in the repository; Git still checks them out with the
# platform's own endings.
#
# NOTE: this only governs files as they are committed from here on. The
# existing CRLF files are NOT renormalised in this pass - that wants its own
# clearly-labelled commit plus a .git-blame-ignore-revs entry, so the noise
# stays in one place forever.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell tooling is run by Windows and stays CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
